      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "<i>In vitro</i>: <i>Acropora tenuis</i> cells of the IVB5 line and symbiosis with the photosynthetic dinoflagellate, <i>Breviolum minutum</i> (Symbiodiniaceae).\nA time-lapse video of symbiotic interactions of coral cells (b and c) and dinoflagellates (x and y). The starting point of observations is shown at 0 h: 00 min: 00 s. <b>(A–J)</b> Serial pictures are taken at time intervals indicated at the bottom. Coral cell b engulfs symbiont x, whereas coral cell c endocytoses symbiont y.",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
      },
